The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if ((dep->flags & DWC3_EP_PENDING_REQUEST)) {
    if (dep->flags & DWC3_EP_TRANSFER_STARTED) {
        dwc3_stop_active_transfer(dwc, dep->number, true);
        dep->flags = DWC3_EP_ENABLED;
    } else {
        u32 cur_uf;
        cur_uf = __dwc3_gadget_get_frame(dwc);
        __dwc3_gadget_start_isoc(dwc, dep, cur_uf);
        dep->flags &= ~DWC3_EP_PENDING_REQUEST;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The simplification in the handling of ISO transfers did not properly manage the state of ongoing transfers, particularly when the `XferInProgress` event occurred. This led to the premature stopping of active transfers and inadequate handling of the transfer state, resulting in a significant performance degradation.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if ((dep->flags & DWC3_EP_BUSY) &&
    !(dep->flags & DWC3_EP_MISSED_ISOC)) {
    WARN_ON_ONCE(!dep->resource_index);
    ret = __dwc3_gadget_kick_transfer(dep, dep->resource_index);
}
```
Reason:
The fix reintroduces the handling of ongoing ISO transfers by checking if the endpoint is busy and not missed, allowing the transfer to continue properly. This ensures that the transfer state is managed correctly, restoring the original performance metrics for ISO transfers.

